"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {"implementer": 1}}, "safety_stops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 2, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "Startup now runs from `lifespan.startup`, and the required check passes: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_lifespan.py tests/test_plugins.py` gives 157 passed, 4 skipped. I read the diff against the spec and found nothing that departs from it. I didn't touch `tests/test_lifespan.py`.\n\n- **`datasette/app.py`:**\n  - `Datasette` has a new idempotent, lock-guarded `_startup_sequence()`. It does the immutable-database table-count precompute and then calls `invoke_startup()`.\n  - `__init__` sets `_setup_db_done` and creates `_startup_lock` in both the normal and `RuntimeError` branches.\n  - `app()` no longer has the local `setup_db`. `AsgiLifespan` now runs `_startup_sequence` on startup, and `AsgiRunOnFirstRequest` keeps it as the fallback.\n- **`datasette/utils/asgi.py`:**\n  - `AsgiLifespan` turns a startup or shutdown exception into `lifespan.startup.failed` or `lifespan.shutdown.failed` instead of letting it escape.\n  - `AsgiRunOnFirstRequest` passes lifespan scopes straight through.\n  - For other scopes it takes a lock, re-checks, runs the hooks, and only then sets `_started`, so concurrent first requests wait for startup to finish.\n- **`datasette/cli.py`:** `serve` calls `ds._startup_sequence()` instead of `ds.invoke_startup()`, with the comment updated.\n\nThe implementer also ran `tests/test_cli.py` and `tests/test_cli_serve_get.py` as a regression check, and they passed (53). I didn't re-run those two.", "ttft_ms": 3001, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 11817, "uuid": "58f2bcc5-990b-47d1-98c8-c03ab8da097a", "ttft_stream_ms": 2426, "time_to_request_ms": 17, "first_content_frame_ms": 2427, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 1}
